a. Obtain approval from the Data Integrity Board to conduct the matching program;b. Develop and enter into a computer matching agreement;c. Publish a matching notice in the Federal Register;d. Independently verify the information produced by the matching program before taking adverse action against an individual, if required; ande. Provide individuals with notice and an opportunity to contest the findings before taking adverse action against an individual.', N'L', 0, NULL, NULL, N'C800_53_R5_V2', NULL, 7527)
