1. develop, disseminate, and annually review and update the configuration management policy and program which defines the purpose of the nuclear facility''s configuration management policy, scope, roles, requirements, responsibilities, and management commitments necessary to provide, with high assurance, that:    a. when a modification to a CDA does not reduce the existing security and    b. any unauthorized or inadvertent modification of a CDA is prevented. The configuration management policy and program must apply to both licensee and vendor personnel.2. develop procedures to facilitate and maintain the configuration management policy and program and associated configuration management controls and measures.3. implement the security controls described in Section 11 of Appendix C to this guide.', N'Configuration Management', N'Configuration Management', 4, NULL, N'Nrc_571', NULL, NULL, 5023, 10, NULL, NULL)
1. develop, disseminate, and annually review and update the configuration management policy and program which defines the purpose of the nuclear facility''s configuration management policy, scope, roles, requirements, responsibilities, and management commitments necessary to provide, with high assurance, that:    a. when a modification to a CDA does not reduce the existing security and    b. any unauthorized or inadvertent modification of a CDA is prevented. The configuration management policy and program must apply to both licensee and vendor personnel.2. develop procedures to facilitate and maintain the configuration management policy and program and associated configuration management controls and measures.3. implement the security controls described in Section 11 of Appendix C to this guide.', N'Configuration Management', N'Configuration Management', 7, NULL, N'Nrc_571', NULL, NULL, 7165, 10, NULL, NULL)
