1. management of user identifiers by the following methods:    a. uniquely identifying each user and application acting as a user    b. verifying the identity of each user and application acting as a user    c. receiving authorization to issue a user identifier from an appropriate organization official    d. ensuring that the user identifier is issued to the intended party    e. disabling user identifier after a predetermined defined time period of inactivity    f. archiving user identifiers2. management of CDA authenticators by the following methods:    a. defining initial authenticator content    b. establishing administrative procedures for initial authenticator distribution for lost, compromised, or damaged authenticators and for revoking authenticators    c. changing default authenticators upon control system installation    d. changing and refreshing authenticators periodically3. implementation of the security controls described in Section 4 of Appendix B to this guide.', N'Identification And Authentication', N'Procedures', 7, NULL, N'Nrc_571', NULL, NULL, 7188, 39, NULL, NULL)
