an-in-the-middle attack are among the most popular ways to manipulate insecure protocols, such as those found in control systems. However, there are mitigation techniques [36] that can be applied to secure the systems through MAC address locking, static tables, encryption, and monitoring.', N'Network Architecture', N'Network Architecture', 8, NULL, N'C800_82', NULL, NULL, 6285, 9, NULL, NULL)
