cal identity theft.• Accurate ePHI may not be available when needed, which can adversely impact your healthcare professionals’ ability to diagnose and treat their patients.Your practice may not be able safeguard its facilities, information system, and ePHI if it does not assure that its other security program documentation is maintained in binders on a shelf or in electronic form.Some potential impacts include:• Unauthorized or inappropriate access to ePHI can compromise the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of your practice’s ePHI.• Unauthorized disclosure, loss, or theft of ePHI can lead to medical identity theft.• Accurate ePHI may not be available when needed, which can adversely impact your healthcare professionals’ ability to diagnose and treat their patients.Your practice may not be able to safeguard its facilities, information system, and ePHI if it does not assure that its policies, procedures, and other security program documentation is retained for at least six (6) years from the date when it was created or last in effect, whichever is longer?Some potential impacts include:• Unauthorized or inappropriate access to ePHI can compromise the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of your practice’s ePHI.• Unauthorized disclosure, loss, or theft of ePHI can lead to medical identity theft.• Accurate ePHI may not be available when needed, which can adversely impact your healthcare professionals’ ability to diagnose and treat their patients.Your practice may not be able to safeguard its facilities, information systems, and ePHI if it does not assure that its policies, procedures and other security program documentation is available to those who need it to perform the responsibilities associated with their role.Some potential impacts include:• Unauthorized or inappropriate access to ePHI can compromise the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of your practice’s ePHI.• Unauthorized disclosure, loss, or theft of ePHI can lead 