Some organizations use commercial tools that evaluate the rule set of network filtering devices to determine whether they are consistent or in conflict, providing an automated sanity check of network filters and search for errors in rule sets or access controls lists (ACLs) that may allow unintended services through the device. Such tools should be run each time significant changes are made to firewall rule sets, router ACLs, or other filtering technologies.', N'Secure Configurations for Network Devices', N'Secure Configurations for Network Devices', 0, NULL, N'CSC_V6', NULL, NULL, 8716, 50, NULL, NULL)
