The organization conducting the inspection/assessment obtains and examines the records of notifications of post-employment requirements for protection of organizational information to ensure the organization being inspected/assessed notifies individuals of applicable, legally binding post-employment requirements for protection of organizational information.CCI DefinitionThe organization being inspected/assessed notifies individuals of applicable, legally binding post-employment requirements for protection of organizational information. The organization must maintain records of notifications of post-employment requirements for protection of organizational information.NIST 800-53 reference PS-6 (3) (a)', N'Personnel Security', N'Personnel Security', 0, NULL, N'CCI_V2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 67, NULL, NULL)
The organization conducting the inspection/assessment obtains and examines the documented process and a sampling of signed acknowledgements to ensure the organization being inspected/assessed requires individuals to sign an acknowledgement of legally binding post-employment requirements for protection of organizational information, if applicable, as part of granting initial access to covered information.CCI DefinitionThe organization being inspected/assessed documents and implements a process to require individuals to sign an acknowledgement of legally binding post-employment requirements for protection of organizational information, if applicable, as part of granting initial access to covered information.NIST 800-53 reference PS-6 (3) (b)', N'Personnel Security', N'Personnel Security', 0, NULL, N'CCI_V2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 67, NULL, NULL)
DoD 5220.22-M, DoD 5220.22-R, DoD 5200.2-R, DoD 8570.01-M and DoDI 3020.41 meet the DoD personnel security requirements including security roles and responsibilities for third-party providers. DoD Components are automatically compliant with this control because they are covered by the DoD level policies, DoD 5220.22-M, DoD 5220.22-R, DoD 5200.2-R, DoD 8570.01-M and DoDI 3020.41.CCI DefinitionDoD 5220.22-M, DoD 5220.22-R, DoD 5200.2-R, DoD 8570.01-M and DoDI 3020.41 meet the DoD personnel security requirements including security roles and responsibilities for third-party providers. DoD Components are automatically compliant with this control because they are covered by the DoD level policies, DoD 5220.22-M, DoD 5220.22-R, DoD 5200.2-R, DoD 8570.01-M and DoDI 3020.41.NIST 800-53 reference PS-7 (a)', N'Personnel Security', N'Personnel Security', 0, NULL, N'CCI_V2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 67, NULL, NULL)
