An Intrusion prevention system (IPS) should be fully deployed throughout the financial institution. Ideally, both host and perimeter IPS exist. The Host IPS should be placed inline (in the direct communication path between source and destination), while the perimeter IPS would be in front of or directly behind the perimeter firewall. Both should be actively analyzing and taking automated actions on all traffic flows that enter the network.', N'Preventative Controls', N'Infrastructure Management', 0, NULL, N'ACET_V1', NULL, NULL, 255, 50, N'Review network topology diagram(s) to determine IPS implementation and placement in the network. 

