A zero-day vulnerability is an unknown exploit in the wild that exposes a vulnerability in software or hardware and can create complicated problems well before anyone realizes something is wrong. A zero-day exploit leaves no opportunity for detection at first. Attackers release malware before a developer has an opportunity to create a patch to fix the vulnerability.', N'Detection, Response, and Mitigation', N'Detection', 0, NULL, N'ACET_V1', NULL, NULL, 463, 58, N'Discuss with management if the financial Institution has a process implemented that can detect and block zero-day attempts and inform management and the incident response team in real-time.', NULL)

